          "id": "doc-f72194b71ba6::sentence-4",
          "documentId": "doc-f72194b71ba6",
          "text": "Evidence 1: What are the adverse effects of infecting children with COVID-19 A complication that has more recently been observed in children can be severe and dangerous. ",
          "start": 241,
          "end": 411,
          "context": "Source URL: https://www.health.harvard.edu/diseases-and-conditions/coronavirus-outbreak-and-kids\n Evidence 1: What are the adverse effects of infecting children with COVID-19 A complication that has more recently been observed in children can be severe and dangerous.  Called multisystem inflammatory syndrome in children (MIS-C), it can lead to life-threatening problems with the heart and other organs in the body. "
